From eaf642d6c3bb65ef0126c4ed332b52c0a63fcfdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knivesbatz <knivesbatz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:22:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add PlayStation (DualShock 4) button prompts in game texts

With a DualShock 4 or another PlayStation controller, the button tags of
the game's hints and tutorials name the PlayStation buttons in place of
the Xbox icons: <a> -> [Cross], <b> -> [Circle], <x> -> [Square],
<y> -> [Triangle], <lb>/<rb> -> [L1]/[R1], <lt>/<rt> -> [L2]/[R2],
<start>/<back> -> [Options]/[Share]. Stick and d-pad icons stay; combo
tags such as <x-left> become <analogleft>+[Square].

controller_prompts = "auto" (default) follows the type SDL reports for
the first connected controller; "xbox" and "playstation" force a style.
The launcher offers it under Settings -> Controls in all seven
languages. Keyboard prompts keep priority in keyboard and mouse mode.

Built on the translation mod's text-table hook, so it works with the
English game text and with translation mods, on both renderers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
